te-temporary-changes-clerks-office-hours.\n\n# Unlawful Detainer (Evictions) Form Packets\n\n## Unlawful Detainer (Evictions) Form Packets\n\nUnlawful Detainer (Eviction) forms\nForm number  | Form name  | Download\n--- | --- | ---\nCM-010  | Civil Case Cover Sheet  | Download CM-010 (PDF)\nUD-101  | Plaintiff’s Mandatory Cover Sheet and Supplemental Allegations – Unlawful Detainer  | Download UD-101 (PDF)\nSUM-130  | Summons – Unlawful Detainer (Eviction)  | Download SUM-130 (PDF)\nUD-100  | Complaint – Unlawful Detainer  | Download UD-100 (PDF)\nPOS-010  | Proof of Service of Summons  | Download POS-010 (PDF)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSUM-130 K SUMMONS—EVICTION  (소환장—명도소송) (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-11/sum130k.pdf)\nciteturn1992search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; SUMMONS—EVICTION ... Top-right court-use box labeled “FOR COURT USE ONLY (법원용)” with form number “SUM-130 K” above it. ... You have 10 DAYS not counting Saturdays and Sundays and other judicial holidays, after this summons and legal papers are served on you to file a written response at this court and have a copy served on the plaintiff. ... January 1, 2026, Mandatory Form\nThe court's lien must be paid before the court dismisses the case.\n</td>\n<td>\n수수료 면제: 제출 수수료를 지불할 수 없는 경우, 서기에게 수수료 면제 양식을 요청하십시오. 주의: 민사 사건에서 $10,000 이상의 합의금 또는 중재판정금이 발생할 경우, 법원은 면제된 수수료 및 비용과 관련하여 해당 금액에 법정담보권을 갖습니다. 법원이 해당 사건을 각하하기 전에 법원의 담보권이 먼저 변제되어야 합니다.\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n1. The name and address of the court is:  \n(법원 이름 및 주소):\n\n<table id=\"e3\">\n<tr>\n<td>CASE NUMBER (사건 번호):</td>\n<td>법원에 제출하지 마십시오</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n2. The name, address, and telephone number of plaintiff's attorney, or plaintiff without an attorney, is: (원고의 변호사 또는 변호사가 없는 원고의 이름, 주소 및 전화번호):\n\nJudicial Council of California, courts.ca.gov  \nRev. January 1, 2026, Mandatory Form  \nCode Civ. Proc., §§ 412.20, 415.45, 1167\n\n소환장—명도소송  \n(불법 점유 / 강제 점유 / 강제 진입)\n\nSUM-130 K, 페이지 1 / 1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFill out forms to start an eviction case | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/eviction-landlord/fill-out)\nciteturn1992search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; To start the eviction case, fill out 4 court forms:    * Summons – Unlawful Detainer—Eviction (form SUM-130)\nDay 3: Tuesday → File on Wednesday (Day 4) if tenant doesn't fix the problem.\n\n  * EXAMPLE: 30-day Notice to quit\n\nNotice delivered Thursday →\nDay 1: Friday → Keep counting calendar days → File on Day 31 if tenant doesn't move out.\n\n### Gather your papers\n\n  * Lease or rental agreement (and any changes the tenant agreed to)\n\n  * Copy of the notice\n\n  * Proof you gave the notice\n\n  * Other proof to show the judge the tenant should move out\n\n⚠️ Eviction cases are detail-heavy. Even small mistakes can make you lose and start over. Get help from a lawyer or self-help center ↗️ (link opens in a new tab).\n\n## How to fill out eviction forms\n\n  * ### Fill out the forms\n\nTo start the eviction case, fill out 4 court forms: \n\n    * Summons – Unlawful Detainer—Eviction (form SUM-130) \n\n    * Complaint – Unlawful Detainer (form UD-100) \n\n    * Civil Case Cover Sheet (form CM-010) \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSummons-Unlawful Detainer-Eviction (form SUM-130) | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/vi/node/899)\nciteturn1992search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # Summons-Unlawful Detainer-Eviction (form SUM-130) ... If you get a Summons (form SUM-130) , this means your landlord started a court case asking a judge to order you to move out - to evict you.\n\nWhat do these papers mean?\n\n# Summons-Unlawful Detainer-Eviction (form SUM-130)\n\n↗️ All court form links open in a new tab.\n\n \n\nIf you get a Summons (form SUM-130) , this means your landlord started a court case asking a judge to order you to move out - to evict you. The Summons comes with another paper called a Complaint. An eviction court case is also called an unlawful detainer case. \n\n## What does this mean for you?\n\nYou have four main choices:\n\n  1. Respond to the eviction case by filing a written response with the court very quickly. This means you're going to participate in the lawsuit and fight the eviction. \n  2. Talk with your landlord and try to come up with an agreement where you can stay in your home. You may be able to work with a mediator who helps people come to an agreement outside of court.\n  3. Move out. But know that if you owe back rent your landlord can still sue you for it in small claims or a civil court case.\n  4. Do nothing. The landlord can evict you without your having a say in the case. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSUM-130 C SUMMONS—EVICTION （传票—驱逐） (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-11/sum130c.pdf)\nciteturn1992search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; SUMMONS—EVICTION ... SUM-130 C ... You have 10 DAYS, not counting Saturdays and Sundays and other judicial holidays, after this summons and legal papers are served on you to file a written response at this court and have a copy served on the plaintiff. ... January 1, 2026, Mandatory Form\n\n还有其他法律要求。您可能需要立即致电律师。如果您不认识任何律师，您可能需要致电律师转介服务处。如果您无法负担律师费用，您可能符合非营利法律服务计划提供的免费法律服务资格。如需查找这些非营利团体，您可以前往加利福尼亚州法律服务网站（www.lawhelpca.org）、加利福尼亚州法院的自助服务中心（selfhelp.courts.ca.gov）或联系您当地的法院或县律师协会。\n\n费用减免：如果您无力支付申请费用，请向书记员索取费用减免表格。注意：如果民事案件的和解或仲裁裁决金额达 $10,000 或以上，法院对减免的费用和成本享有法定留置权。在法院驳回案件之前，必须先支付该笔留置费用。\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n1. The name and address of the court is:  \n（法院名称及地址为：）：\n\n<table id=\"e2\">\n<tr>\n<td>CASE NUMBER（案件编号）：</td>\n<td>不得向法院提交</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n2. The name, address, and telephone number of p